  "answer": "This feature request has been filed before. Light Switch currently only switches the Windows light/dark mode and doesn't change the wallpaper. PowerToys#42401 is the main tracking issue for changing the wallpaper along with the theme. PowerToys#42984 asked for the same thing with separate slideshow folders for light and dark mode, and it was closed as a duplicate of #42401. PowerToys#42436 asks for per-mode wallpapers or themes. In that ticket a contributor said they had a prototype wallpaper-switching implementation and linked PR #42624. Please add your use case, including the folder/slideshow idea, as a comment or thumbs-up on #42401 rather than opening a new issue. The archive shows no released feature yet. Until one ships, people use a third-party tool such as Auto Dark Mode, or a scheduled task that runs a wallpaper command. PowerToys#46722 also asks for Light Switch to run custom commands on a mode change, which would cover the same need."
